      "adventure_name": "The Drowned Bell",
      "adventure_description": "On still nights, the people of Hollin Ferry hear a bell tolling under the Grey Mere, from the sunken priory on Corvane's Holm. Since it began, the drowned dead have been seen walking on the causeway. An introductory adventure for three to six characters of first level.",
      "town_name": "Hollin Ferry",
      "town_description": "A huddle of reed-thatched houses and smokehouses on the shore of the Grey Mere. A flat-bottomed ferry crosses to Corvane's Holm when the ferryman can be paid to go. The temple of the Lantern stands at the top of the street, and its own bell has hung silent since the drowned bell began to toll.",
      "town_services": [
        "Ostler's store: weapons, armour, and adventuring gear",
        "Temple of the Lantern: cure light wounds, cure serious wounds, cure disease, neutralize poison, remove curse, and raise dead",
        "Widow Marl, moneychanger: buys gems, jewellery, and coin",
        "The Smoked Eel: beds, hot food, and a quiet corner to study spells"
